# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use Qiskit and IBM Quantum Compute Service developer tools to profile, customize, and inspect your experiment settings and runtime environment."
msgstr "Gunakan tool developer Qiskit dan IBM Quantum Compute Service untuk memprofil, menyesuaikan, dan memeriksa pengaturan eksperimen serta runtime environment kamu."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tools to profile, customize, and inspect experiments"
msgstr "Tool untuk memprofil, menyesuaikan, dan memeriksa eksperimen"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"tutorials/profiling-tools.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Usage estimate: 10 minutes on a Heron r2 processor (NOTE: This is an estimate only. Your runtime might vary.)*\n"
msgstr "*Perkiraan penggunaan: 10 menit pada prosesor Heron r2 (CATATAN: Ini hanya perkiraan. Waktu runtime kamu mungkin berbeda.)*\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To get good results from a quantum computer, you need more than a well-designed circuit. The device's current condition, how your circuit is scheduled, the noise that the circuit experiences, and when and how your job runs on the quantum processing unit (QPU) all affect the quality of your results. Qiskit and IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service offer a growing set of developer tools that expose this information. You can use these tools to act on that information before you commit QPU time to a full experiment, and to debug a finished experiment.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mendapat hasil bagus dari komputer kuantum, kamu butuh lebih dari sekadar circuit yang dirancang dengan baik. Kondisi device saat ini, cara circuit dijadwalkan, noise yang dialami circuit, serta kapan dan bagaimana job kamu berjalan di quantum processing unit (QPU) semuanya memengaruhi kualitas hasil. Qiskit dan IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service menawarkan kumpulan tool developer yang terus bertambah dan mengungkap informasi ini. Kamu bisa memakai tool ini untuk bertindak berdasarkan informasi itu sebelum mengeluarkan waktu QPU untuk eksperimen penuh, dan untuk men-debug eksperimen yang sudah selesai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses a single end-to-end experiment to show how to combine these tools at each stage of a typical development workflow. Not every tool is useful for every experiment, so choose the tools that address the questions that you have about your own workload.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini memakai satu eksperimen end-to-end untuk menunjukkan cara menggabungkan tool-tool ini di setiap tahap alur kerja pengembangan yang umum. Tidak semua tool berguna untuk setiap eksperimen, jadi pilih tool yang menjawab pertanyaan yang kamu punya tentang workload-mu sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Alur kerjanya sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare a mirror circuit of a Trotterized time evolution of a linear transverse-field Ising model.\n"
msgstr "Siapkan circuit mirror dari evolusi waktu Trotter model Ising medan-transversal linear.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select a backend with an alternative calibration data set that is designed for error mitigation methods based on a noise model.\n"
msgstr "Pilih backend dengan set data kalibrasi alternatif yang dirancang untuk metode mitigasi error berbasis model noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run device benchmarking experiments so that the transpiler uses up-to-date device properties when it selects a layout.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan eksperimen benchmarking device agar transpiler memakai properti device terbaru saat memilih layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect the timing information of the scheduled circuit.\n"
msgstr "Periksa informasi timing dari circuit yang dijadwalkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn Pauli-Lindblad and readout noise models for the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Pelajari model noise Pauli-Lindblad dan readout untuk circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run noiseless, unmitigated, and mitigated local simulations. The noisy simulations use the learned noise model to show how much improvement you might gain from the selected error mitigation methods. This tutorial uses probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) and Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX).\n"
msgstr "Jalankan simulasi lokal tanpa noise, tanpa mitigasi, dan dengan mitigasi. Simulasi ber-noise memakai model noise yang dipelajari untuk menunjukkan seberapa besar peningkatan yang mungkin kamu peroleh dari metode mitigasi error yang dipilih. Tutorial ini memakai probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) dan Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get a usage estimate without running on a QPU, to check whether you need to adjust the experiment to fit your budget.\n"
msgstr "Dapatkan perkiraan penggunaan tanpa menjalankan di QPU, untuk memeriksa apakah kamu perlu menyesuaikan eksperimen agar sesuai anggaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '8. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start a session and trigger calibration so that the experiment uses the most recent calibration data.\n"
msgstr "Mulai session dan picu kalibrasi agar eksperimen memakai data kalibrasi terbaru.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '9. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the experiment on the QPU by using Estimator, and compare the hardware results with the simulated preview.\n"
msgstr "Jalankan eksperimen di QPU dengan Estimator, dan bandingkan hasil hardware dengan pratinjau simulasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '10. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect the execution spans to see whether there are significant gaps between groups of executions (chunks).\n"
msgstr "Periksa execution span untuk melihat apakah ada celah signifikan di antara kelompok eksekusi (chunk).\n"

