# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Specify a circuit and observable {#step-1-specify-a-circuit-and-observable}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Tentukan circuit dan observable {#step-1-specify-a-circuit-and-observable}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare a mirror circuit of a Trotterized time evolution of a linear transverse-field Ising model. Mirror the circuit to cancel the circuit unitary and form an identity circuit. Because the ideal output is the all-zero state, the ideal expectation value of each single-qubit $Z$ observable is 1. Mirroring also doubles the circuit depth, which amplifies the effect of noise.\n"
msgstr "Siapkan circuit mirror dari evolusi waktu Trotter model Ising medan-transversal linear. Cerminkan circuit untuk membatalkan unitary circuit dan membentuk circuit identitas. Karena keluaran idealnya adalah state semua-nol, nilai ekspektasi ideal tiap observable $Z$ satu-qubit adalah 1. Pencerminan juga menggandakan kedalaman circuit, yang memperkuat efek noise.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/caa280da-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/caa280da-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimalkan untuk eksekusi di hardware kuantum {#step-2-optimize-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.1 Use alternative calibration if applicable {#21-use-alternative-calibration-if-applicable}"
msgstr "2.1 Gunakan kalibrasi alternatif jika berlaku {#21-use-alternative-calibration-if-applicable}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM&reg; calibrates its QPUs periodically for good performance across general use cases. Some workloads, however, benefit from instructions whose parameters are tuned differently. For more information, refer to [Specially calibrated instructions](/guides/custom-calibration).\n"
msgstr "IBM&reg; mengalibrasi QPU-nya secara berkala untuk performa yang baik di berbagai kasus penggunaan umum. Namun, beberapa workload diuntungkan oleh instruksi yang parameternya disetel berbeda. Untuk informasi lebih lanjut, lihat [Specially calibrated instructions](/guides/custom-calibration).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses an alternative calibration data set called `slow_gates_ac`. This calibration contains a slower `cz` gate and modulates the two-level system (TLS) bias to stabilize device errors over time. These changes benefit error mitigation methods that rely on a learned noise model. The `slow_gates_ac` calibration is available only on Heron QPUs. If you run on a Nighthawk QPU, use `slow_gates` instead.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini memakai set data kalibrasi alternatif bernama `slow_gates_ac`. Kalibrasi ini berisi gate `cz` yang lebih lambat dan memodulasi bias two-level system (TLS) untuk menstabilkan error device dari waktu ke waktu. Perubahan ini menguntungkan metode mitigasi error yang bergantung pada model noise yang dipelajari. Kalibrasi `slow_gates_ac` hanya tersedia di QPU Heron. Jika kamu menjalankan di QPU Nighthawk, pakai `slow_gates` sebagai gantinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.2 Run real-time device benchmarking {#22-run-real-time-device-benchmarking}"
msgstr "2.2 Jalankan benchmarking device real-time {#22-run-real-time-device-benchmarking}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One of the most critical stages of transpilation is layout selection, which maps virtual qubits in a circuit to physical qubits on the target device. A good layout minimizes the number of SWAP operations needed and places the circuit on the best-performing qubits, so the quality of the initial layout can significantly affect the quality of your results.\n"
msgstr "Salah satu tahap transpilasi yang paling kritis adalah pemilihan layout, yang memetakan qubit virtual di circuit ke qubit fisik di device target. Layout yang baik meminimalkan jumlah operasi SWAP yang dibutuhkan dan menempatkan circuit pada qubit dengan performa terbaik, jadi kualitas layout awal bisa sangat memengaruhi kualitas hasil kamu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Periodic benchmarking routines run on every IBM QPU to report the current performance of its qubits: relaxation times ($T_1$), coherence times ($T_2$), readout errors, and one- and two-qubit gate errors. The Qiskit transpiler uses these metrics during layout selection.\n"
msgstr "Rutinitas benchmarking berkala berjalan di setiap QPU IBM untuk melaporkan performa terkini qubit-nya: waktu relaksasi ($T_1$), waktu koherensi ($T_2$), error readout, dan error gate satu- dan dua-qubit. Transpiler Qiskit memakai metrik ini saat memilih layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The properties of superconducting qubits, however, can drift on shorter timescales, and transient defects, known as TLSs, can temporarily degrade a qubit that performed well at calibration time. If the transpiler uses outdated information, it cannot select the best layout. Therefore, it can be worthwhile to spend some QPU time to characterize the device before you select a layout.\n"
msgstr "Namun, properti qubit superkonduktor bisa bergeser dalam skala waktu yang lebih pendek, dan cacat sementara, yang dikenal sebagai TLS, dapat menurunkan sementara kualitas qubit yang tadinya bagus saat kalibrasi. Jika transpiler memakai informasi yang usang, ia tidak bisa memilih layout terbaik. Karena itu, mungkin layak mengorbankan sedikit waktu QPU untuk mengkarakterisasi device sebelum kamu memilih layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Refer to the [Refresh backend properties with real-time benchmarking](/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking) tutorial for a detailed walk-through.\n"
"The characterization suite builds several experiments, submits multiple jobs, and fits the results. This process can take a few minutes in total. Enable INFO-level logging so that each stage prints its progress as it runs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lihat tutorial [Refresh backend properties with real-time benchmarking](/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking) untuk panduan lengkapnya.\n"
"Suite karakterisasi membangun beberapa eksperimen, mengirim banyak job, dan mem-fit hasilnya. Proses ini bisa memakan beberapa menit secara total. Aktifkan logging level INFO agar setiap tahap mencetak progresnya saat berjalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`BackendCharacterization` is a convenience class that runs the characterization experiments of your choice, analyzes the results, and returns an updated `Backend` object that you can pass to the transpiler.\n"
msgstr "`BackendCharacterization` adalah kelas praktis yang menjalankan eksperimen karakterisasi pilihan kamu, menganalisis hasilnya, dan mengembalikan objek `Backend` yang sudah diperbarui, yang bisa kamu teruskan ke transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You might see a warning that a backend was passed in as the mode while a batch is open. This warning is expected, and you can safely ignore it.\n"
msgstr "Kamu mungkin melihat peringatan bahwa sebuah backend diteruskan sebagai mode sementara sebuah batch terbuka. Peringatan ini wajar, dan kamu aman mengabaikannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.3 Transpile to ISA {#23-transpile-to-isa}"
msgstr "2.3 Transpile ke ISA {#23-transpile-to-isa}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transform the circuit and observables to match the backend's instruction set architecture (ISA) by using the refreshed device properties.\n"
msgstr "Ubah circuit dan observable agar sesuai dengan instruction set architecture (ISA) backend, dengan memakai properti device yang sudah disegarkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.4 Visualize circuit timing {#24-visualize-circuit-timing}"
msgstr "2.4 Visualisasikan timing circuit {#24-visualize-circuit-timing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In addition to the instructions in a circuit, you might want to visualize the circuit's schedule, to find idle time on qubits or inefficient instruction alignment. You can get the most detailed and accurate timing information from IBM Quantum Compute Service by using dry-run mode.\n"
msgstr "Selain instruksi dalam circuit, kamu mungkin ingin memvisualisasikan jadwal circuit, untuk menemukan waktu menganggur pada qubit atau penyelarasan instruksi yang tidak efisien. Kamu bisa mendapat informasi timing paling detail dan akurat dari IBM Quantum Compute Service dengan memakai mode dry-run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuit in this tutorial is static, so its schedule is not very informative. You can get similar timing information locally from the circuit and the backend properties, for example by using the [timeline drawer](/guides/visualize-circuit-timing) built into Qiskit. This tutorial includes this step to show how to request and visualize the timing information. Timing information from the service is most useful for [dynamic circuits](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow). Dynamic circuits contain mid-circuit measurements, conditional operations, and feedforward, which add implicit operations such as broadcasting measurement results and determining branches. The timing of these operations cannot be determined from the circuit and backend properties alone.\n"
msgstr "Circuit dalam tutorial ini bersifat statis, jadi jadwalnya tidak terlalu informatif. Kamu bisa mendapatkan informasi timing serupa secara lokal dari circuit dan properti backend, misalnya dengan [timeline drawer](/guides/visualize-circuit-timing) bawaan Qiskit. Tutorial ini menyertakan langkah ini untuk menunjukkan cara meminta dan memvisualisasikan informasi timing. Informasi timing dari layanan paling berguna untuk [dynamic circuit](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow). Dynamic circuit berisi pengukuran di tengah circuit, operasi kondisional, dan feedforward, yang menambahkan operasi implisit seperti menyiarkan hasil pengukuran dan menentukan cabang. Timing operasi-operasi ini tidak bisa ditentukan dari circuit dan properti backend saja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Refer to [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing) for more information.\n"
"Scheduled circuit timing is available only for Sampler and Executor jobs, so the following cell submits the circuit in dry-run mode by using Sampler. Jobs that you submit in dry-run mode do not run on real QPUs and are not charged.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lihat [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"
"Timing circuit terjadwal hanya tersedia untuk job Sampler dan Executor, jadi sel berikut mengirimkan circuit dalam mode dry-run menggunakan Sampler. Job yang kamu kirim dalam mode dry-run tidak berjalan di QPU sungguhan dan tidak dikenai biaya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
