# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Apply error mitigation and test locally {#step-3-apply-error-mitigation-and-test-locally}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Terapkan error mitigation dan uji secara lokal {#step-3-apply-error-mitigation-and-test-locally}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 Cliffordize the circuit {#31-cliffordize-the-circuit}"
msgstr "3.1 Cliffordize circuit {#31-cliffordize-the-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cost of general noisy simulation grows exponentially with the number of qubits, and most laptops cannot simulate more than about 32 qubits. Therefore, first convert the circuit to a Clifford circuit, which a stabilizer simulator can handle far more efficiently. The conversion rounds each rotation angle to a Clifford angle, so the simulated circuit approximates the original circuit rather than reproducing it.\n"
msgstr "Biaya simulasi noisy secara umum tumbuh secara eksponensial terhadap jumlah qubit, dan sebagian besar laptop tidak bisa mensimulasikan lebih dari sekitar 32 qubit. Karena itu, ubah dulu circuit menjadi circuit Clifford, yang bisa ditangani simulator stabilizer jauh lebih efisien. Konversi ini membulatkan setiap sudut rotasi ke sudut Clifford, sehingga circuit yang disimulasikan hanya mendekati circuit aslinya, bukan mereproduksinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Apply PEC with TREX {#32-apply-pec-with-trex}"
msgstr "3.2 Terapkan PEC dengan TREX {#32-apply-pec-with-trex}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It can be difficult to select error mitigation methods that balance cost and accuracy for your specific experiment. You can use the `select-error-mitigation` AI agent skill to analyze the available methods for your workload. The skill presents a summary report that explains whether each method was selected and why.\n"
msgstr "Memilih metode error mitigation yang menyeimbangkan biaya dan akurasi untuk eksperimen spesifikmu bisa jadi sulit. Kamu bisa memakai skill agen AI `select-error-mitigation` untuk menganalisis metode yang tersedia untuk workload kamu. Skill ini menyajikan laporan ringkasan yang menjelaskan apakah setiap metode dipilih dan alasannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Refer to the [Qiskit AI skills](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) GitHub repository for more information.\n"
"This tutorial uses PEC with TREX directly, so that you can complete it without an AI agent.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lihat repositori GitHub [Qiskit AI skills](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"
"Tutorial ini memakai PEC dengan TREX secara langsung, jadi kamu bisa menyelesaikannya tanpa agen AI.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC is a technique that mitigates quantum noise when you calculate the expectation values of observables. Under ideal conditions, PEC can produce an unbiased estimate of the expectation values. It learns the noise of each layer of two-qubit gates, then runs an ensemble of circuits that, on average, apply the inverse of that noise. PEC uses Pauli twirling to tailor the noise into a Pauli channel, which can be learned and inverted efficiently.\n"
msgstr "PEC adalah teknik yang memitigasi noise kuantum saat kamu menghitung nilai ekspektasi observable. Dalam kondisi ideal, PEC bisa menghasilkan estimasi nilai ekspektasi yang tidak bias. PEC mempelajari noise tiap layer Gate dua-qubit, lalu menjalankan ensemble circuit yang, secara rata-rata, menerapkan invers dari noise tersebut. PEC memakai Pauli twirling untuk menyesuaikan noise menjadi channel Pauli, yang bisa dipelajari dan diinvers secara efisien.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice, PEC is only as accurate as the learned noise model. The sparse Pauli-Lindblad model includes only one- and two-qubit error terms on neighboring qubits, and it cannot fully capture effects such as crosstalk between distant qubits or time-correlated errors. The device noise can also drift between noise learning and execution. PEC does not cancel noise that the model misses, and it overcompensates for noise that the model overestimates. Therefore, mitigated results can still deviate from the ideal values in either direction.\n"
msgstr "Dalam praktiknya, PEC hanya seakurat model noise yang dipelajari. Model sparse Pauli-Lindblad hanya menyertakan suku error satu- dan dua-qubit pada qubit bertetangga, dan tidak bisa sepenuhnya menangkap efek seperti crosstalk antar qubit yang berjauhan atau error yang berkorelasi waktu. Noise perangkat juga bisa bergeser antara pembelajaran noise dan eksekusi. PEC tidak membatalkan noise yang terlewat oleh model, dan ia mengompensasi berlebihan noise yang diestimasi terlalu tinggi oleh model. Karena itu, hasil yang sudah dimitigasi masih bisa menyimpang dari nilai ideal ke kedua arah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"TREX is a technique that mitigates measurement errors, and is useful when you estimate the expectation values of Pauli observables. It relies on measurement twirling, which diagonalizes the readout-error transfer matrix and makes it easy to invert. TREX learns a rescaling term from the diagonal noise channel by measuring twirled calibration circuits that are initialized in the zero state.\n"
"You can enable both PEC and TREX by setting Estimator options. This tutorial uses the client-side implementations of the Qiskit SamplerV2 and EstimatorV2 interfaces, which were introduced in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0. These client-side primitives perform most of the pre- and post-processing locally and delegate execution to the Executor primitive. When the primitives run on the client side, you get greater transparency, faster feedback when you debug, and finer control.\n"
msgstr ""
"TREX adalah teknik yang memitigasi error pengukuran, dan berguna saat kamu mengestimasi nilai ekspektasi observable Pauli. TREX mengandalkan measurement twirling, yang mendiagonalkan matriks transfer readout-error sehingga mudah diinvers. TREX mempelajari suku penskalaan ulang dari channel noise diagonal dengan mengukur circuit kalibrasi ter-twirl yang diinisialisasi dalam state nol.\n"
"Kamu bisa mengaktifkan PEC dan TREX sekaligus dengan mengatur opsi Estimator. Tutorial ini memakai implementasi sisi klien dari antarmuka Qiskit SamplerV2 dan EstimatorV2, yang diperkenalkan di `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0. Primitive sisi klien ini melakukan sebagian besar pra- dan pasca-pemrosesan secara lokal dan mendelegasikan eksekusi ke primitive Executor. Saat primitive berjalan di sisi klien, kamu mendapat transparansi lebih besar, umpan balik lebih cepat saat debugging, dan kontrol yang lebih halus.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The client-side primitives implement the same API as the legacy server-side primitives. Therefore, you can usually switch to the client-side primitives by changing only the import statement.\n"
"Enable INFO-level logging to see the progress of client-side pre- and post-processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primitive sisi klien mengimplementasikan API yang sama dengan primitive sisi server lama. Karena itu, biasanya kamu bisa beralih ke primitive sisi klien hanya dengan mengubah pernyataan import.\n"
"Aktifkan logging level INFO untuk melihat progres pra- dan pasca-pemrosesan sisi klien.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.3 Learn noise models and run the Cliffordized circuit {#33-learn-noise-models-and-run-the-cliffordized-circuit}"
msgstr "3.3 Pelajari model noise dan jalankan circuit yang sudah di-Cliffordize {#33-learn-noise-models-and-run-the-cliffordized-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both PEC and TREX require noise learning, which you can do with `NoiseLearnerV3`. The steps are as follows:\n"
msgstr "PEC dan TREX sama-sama memerlukan pembelajaran noise, yang bisa kamu lakukan dengan `NoiseLearnerV3`. Langkah-langkahnya sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find the unique two-qubit gate layers and measurement layers in the circuit, for the Pauli-Lindblad and TREX protocols, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Temukan layer Gate dua-qubit dan layer pengukuran yang unik di circuit, masing-masing untuk protokol Pauli-Lindblad dan TREX.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the layers to `NoiseLearnerV3` to learn the noise models.\n"
msgstr "Berikan layer tersebut ke `NoiseLearnerV3` untuk mempelajari model noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convert the learned noise models to Pauli-Lindblad maps.\n"
msgstr "Ubah model noise yang dipelajari menjadi peta Pauli-Lindblad.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Estimator does not use a pre-learned TREX noise model. Instead, it performs its own TREX learning. The following code learns both models anyway, because the noisy simulation uses the learned readout model.\n"
msgstr "Estimator tidak memakai model noise TREX yang sudah dipelajari sebelumnya. Sebaliknya, ia melakukan pembelajaran TREX sendiri. Kode berikut tetap mempelajari kedua model, karena simulasi noisy memakai model readout yang dipelajari.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Refer to [Noise learning helper](/guides/noise-learning) for more information about `NoiseLearnerV3`.\n"
"In addition to the noise-learning experiment, run the Cliffordized circuit on the QPU. This step is not always necessary, but it provides a comparison for the simulated results in Step 3.4.4. Run both in a batch to minimize how much the noise profile drifts between the two.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lihat [Noise learning helper](/guides/noise-learning) untuk informasi lebih lanjut tentang `NoiseLearnerV3`.\n"
"Selain eksperimen pembelajaran noise, jalankan circuit yang sudah di-Cliffordize di QPU. Langkah ini tidak selalu diperlukan, tapi memberi pembanding untuk hasil simulasi di Langkah 3.4.4. Jalankan keduanya dalam satu batch untuk meminimalkan pergeseran profil noise di antara keduanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4 Perform local simulation {#34-perform-local-simulation}"
msgstr "3.4 Lakukan simulasi lokal {#34-perform-local-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `qiskit-ibm-runtime` local mode, you can perform both noiseless and noisy simulations locally with minimal code changes. Use local mode to verify syntactic correctness, compare the effects of different mitigation methods, and check how well the learned noise model agrees with hardware results.\n"
msgstr "Dengan mode lokal `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, kamu bisa melakukan simulasi noiseless maupun noisy secara lokal dengan perubahan kode yang minimal. Pakai mode lokal untuk memverifikasi kebenaran sintaksis, membandingkan efek berbagai metode mitigasi, dan memeriksa seberapa cocok model noise yang dipelajari dengan hasil hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Local mode uses largely the same interface as QPU execution. In most cases, you need to change only the backend that you pass when you initialize the primitive, and then rerun the same code. Each of the following subsections creates its own `Estimator` instance, so you can run them without changing a previous cell.\n"
msgstr "Mode lokal memakai antarmuka yang hampir sama dengan eksekusi QPU. Dalam banyak kasus, kamu hanya perlu mengubah backend yang diberikan saat menginisialisasi primitive, lalu menjalankan ulang kode yang sama. Setiap subbagian berikut membuat instance `Estimator` sendiri, jadi kamu bisa menjalankannya tanpa mengubah sel sebelumnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refer to [Local mode](/guides/local-testing-mode) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Lihat [Local mode](/guides/local-testing-mode) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4.1 Run a noiseless simulation {#341-run-a-noiseless-simulation}"
msgstr "3.4.1 Jalankan simulasi noiseless {#341-run-a-noiseless-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4.2 Run a noisy simulation with the learned Pauli-Lindblad model {#342-run-a-noisy-simulation-with-the-learned-pauli-lindblad-model}"
msgstr "3.4.2 Jalankan simulasi noisy dengan model Pauli-Lindblad yang dipelajari {#342-run-a-noisy-simulation-with-the-learned-pauli-lindblad-model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Do not use a fake backend or a Qiskit Aer noise model if you plan to use the learned Pauli-Lindblad noise model in your local simulation. If you do, the simulation applies the noise twice.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Jangan pakai fake backend atau model noise Qiskit Aer jika kamu berencana memakai model noise Pauli-Lindblad yang dipelajari dalam simulasi lokal. Kalau dipakai, simulasi akan menerapkan noise dua kali.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4.3 Run a noisy simulation with PEC and TREX {#343-run-a-noisy-simulation-with-pec-and-trex}"
msgstr "3.4.3 Jalankan simulasi noisy dengan PEC dan TREX {#343-run-a-noisy-simulation-with-pec-and-trex}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.4.4 Compare the simulation results {#344-compare-the-simulation-results}"
msgstr "3.4.4 Bandingkan hasil simulasi {#344-compare-the-simulation-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore frameon sharey */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot the expectation value of each single-qubit $Z$ observable from the three simulations, together with the unmitigated QPU result for the same Clifford circuit from Step 3.3. Because the circuit is a mirror circuit, every ideal value is 1. The error bars show the standard error that Estimator reports for each value.\n"
msgstr "Plot nilai ekspektasi setiap observable $Z$ satu-qubit dari tiga simulasi, bersama hasil QPU tanpa mitigasi untuk circuit Clifford yang sama dari Langkah 3.3. Karena circuit ini adalah mirror circuit, setiap nilai idealnya adalah 1. Error bar menunjukkan standard error yang dilaporkan Estimator untuk tiap nilai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The closer the unmitigated simulation is to the unmitigated QPU result, the better the learned noise model describes the hardware. Use this comparison as a check before you spend QPU time on the mitigated experiment. If the two results disagree significantly, PEC is also unlikely to get close to the ideal values on hardware. In that case, consider relearning the noise model or selecting a different layout. You can also relearn the noise model with different `NoiseLearnerV3` options, such as more randomizations or additional layer-pair depths, and check whether the agreement improves. For example, in Step 3.3 this tutorial sets `num_randomizations` to 64 instead of the default value of 32, because the additional randomizations improved the agreement for this circuit.\n"
msgstr "Semakin dekat simulasi tanpa mitigasi dengan hasil QPU tanpa mitigasi, semakin baik model noise yang dipelajari menggambarkan hardware. Pakai perbandingan ini sebagai pemeriksaan sebelum kamu menghabiskan waktu QPU untuk eksperimen dengan mitigasi. Kalau kedua hasil berbeda jauh, PEC juga kecil kemungkinannya bisa mendekati nilai ideal di hardware. Dalam kasus itu, pertimbangkan untuk mempelajari ulang model noise atau memilih layout lain. Kamu juga bisa mempelajari ulang model noise dengan opsi `NoiseLearnerV3` yang berbeda, seperti lebih banyak randomisasi atau kedalaman layer-pair tambahan, lalu periksa apakah kecocokannya membaik. Misalnya, di Langkah 3.3 tutorial ini mengatur `num_randomizations` ke 64 alih-alih nilai default 32, karena randomisasi tambahan memperbaiki kecocokan untuk circuit ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`NoiseLearnerV3` runs a standard learning protocol. For full control over the learning experiment, you can build your own with [Qiskit noise learning](/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/guides/workflow).\n"
msgstr "`NoiseLearnerV3` menjalankan protokol pembelajaran standar. Untuk kontrol penuh atas eksperimen pembelajaran, kamu bisa membuatnya sendiri dengan [Qiskit noise learning](/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/guides/workflow).\n"

