msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/2e4cb660-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.5 Estimate usage {#35-estimate-usage}"
msgstr "3.5 Estimasi penggunaan {#35-estimate-usage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The main purpose of dry-run mode is to estimate usage. Unlike local mode, dry-run mode submits the job to IBM Quantum Compute Service, which returns an accurate usage estimate but **random result data**. Dry-run jobs do not run on real QPUs and do not consume any QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Tujuan utama mode dry-run adalah mengestimasi penggunaan. Berbeda dengan mode lokal, mode dry-run mengirim job ke IBM Quantum Compute Service, yang mengembalikan estimasi penggunaan yang akurat tetapi **data hasil acak**. Job dry-run tidak berjalan di QPU sungguhan dan tidak memakai waktu QPU sama sekali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs are not available on the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
msgstr "Job dry-run tidak tersedia di paket Open atau Pay-As-You-Go.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refer to [Dry-run jobs](/guides/dry-run-jobs) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Lihat [Dry-run jobs](/guides/dry-run-jobs) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Run on hardware {#step-4-run-on-hardware}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Jalankan di hardware {#step-4-run-on-hardware}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.1 Initialize a session and run calibration {#41-initialize-a-session-and-run-calibration}"
msgstr "4.1 Inisialisasi session dan jalankan kalibrasi {#41-initialize-a-session-and-run-calibration}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "QPU calibration optimizes many parameters that define the electrical signals that drive the quantum gates and operations. Calibration jobs run throughout the day between user jobs, but not during an active session. These parameters can drift within a short period of time. For the best possible results, consider triggering calibration at the start of a session, or periodically during a long-running session.\n"
msgstr "Kalibrasi QPU mengoptimalkan banyak parameter yang menentukan sinyal listrik penggerak Gate dan operasi kuantum. Job kalibrasi berjalan sepanjang hari di sela job pengguna, tetapi tidak saat session aktif. Parameter ini bisa bergeser dalam waktu singkat. Untuk hasil terbaik, pertimbangkan memicu kalibrasi di awal session, atau secara berkala selama session yang berjalan lama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Currently, only readout calibration is supported, and it takes approximately five minutes of wall-clock time.\n"
msgstr "Saat ini hanya kalibrasi readout yang didukung, dan memakan waktu sekitar lima menit wall-clock.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.2 Run on hardware with Estimator {#42-run-on-hardware-with-estimator}"
msgstr "4.2 Jalankan di hardware dengan Estimator {#42-run-on-hardware-with-estimator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following cells run three jobs in the batch or session:\n"
msgstr "Sel-sel berikut menjalankan tiga job dalam batch atau session:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A noise-learning experiment to refresh the noise model. This experiment is useful if you expect the noise model from Step 3.3 to be outdated when the Estimator job runs. In a batch, the Estimator jobs can run much later than the noise-learning job, because jobs from other users can run on the QPU between them. A session gives your workload exclusive access to the QPU, so the noise model is more likely to still be accurate when the experiment runs.\n"
msgstr "Eksperimen pembelajaran noise untuk menyegarkan model noise. Eksperimen ini berguna jika kamu memperkirakan model noise dari Langkah 3.3 sudah usang saat job Estimator berjalan. Dalam batch, job Estimator bisa berjalan jauh setelah job pembelajaran noise, karena job pengguna lain bisa berjalan di QPU di antara keduanya. Session memberi workload kamu akses eksklusif ke QPU, jadi model noise lebih mungkin masih akurat saat eksperimen berjalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The experiment with mitigation.\n"
msgstr "Eksperimen dengan mitigasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The experiment without mitigation, for comparison.\n"
msgstr "Eksperimen tanpa mitigasi, sebagai pembanding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot the mitigated and unmitigated hardware results together with the ideal values. Because the circuit is a mirror circuit, every ideal value is 1, so the distance between each point and the dashed line shows the remaining error. Any remaining deviation from the ideal value, whether above or below it, reflects the statistical uncertainty of PEC and the limits of the learned noise model described in Step 3.2.\n"
msgstr "Plot hasil hardware dengan dan tanpa mitigasi bersama nilai ideal. Karena circuit ini adalah mirror circuit, setiap nilai idealnya adalah 1, jadi jarak antara tiap titik dan garis putus-putus menunjukkan error yang tersisa. Setiap deviasi yang tersisa dari nilai ideal, baik di atas maupun di bawahnya, mencerminkan ketidakpastian statistik PEC dan batas model noise yang dipelajari seperti dijelaskan di Langkah 3.2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To further improve the results, you can try the following:\n"
msgstr "Untuk memperbaiki hasil lebih lanjut, kamu bisa mencoba hal berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Increase the number of shots or randomizations to reduce the statistical uncertainty of the mitigated estimates. The cost grows with the PEC sampling overhead.\n"
msgstr "Tambah jumlah shot atau randomisasi untuk mengurangi ketidakpastian statistik estimasi yang dimitigasi. Biayanya naik sesuai overhead sampling PEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Relearn the noise model immediately before the experiment, in the same session, to reduce the effect of noise drift.\n"
msgstr "Pelajari ulang model noise tepat sebelum eksperimen, dalam session yang sama, untuk mengurangi efek pergeseran noise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise model more precisely by increasing the `num_randomizations`, `shots_per_randomization`, or `layer_pair_depths` options of `NoiseLearnerV3`. Errors in the learned rates bias the mitigated results, and additional PEC shots do not remove this bias.\n"
msgstr "Pelajari model noise dengan lebih presisi dengan menaikkan opsi `num_randomizations`, `shots_per_randomization`, atau `layer_pair_depths` dari `NoiseLearnerV3`. Error pada laju yang dipelajari membiaskan hasil yang dimitigasi, dan shot PEC tambahan tidak menghilangkan bias ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add [non-Markovian error checks](/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks) to detect shots that are likely corrupted by non-Markovian errors, which the learned noise model does not describe. Then discard those shots by postselection. Apply the same checks when you learn the noise model, by using the `bit_flip_checks` options of `NoiseLearnerV3`. Otherwise, the learned model includes errors that postselection removes from the experiment, and PEC overcompensates for them. Stricter postselection discards more shots, so balance the accuracy gain against the number of shots that you keep.\n"
msgstr "Tambahkan [non-Markovian error checks](/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks) untuk mendeteksi shot yang kemungkinan rusak akibat error non-Markovian, yang tidak digambarkan oleh model noise yang dipelajari. Lalu buang shot tersebut lewat postselection. Terapkan pemeriksaan yang sama saat mempelajari model noise, dengan opsi `bit_flip_checks` dari `NoiseLearnerV3`. Kalau tidak, model yang dipelajari memuat error yang dihapus postselection dari eksperimen, dan PEC mengompensasinya secara berlebihan. Postselection yang lebih ketat membuang lebih banyak shot, jadi seimbangkan peningkatan akurasi dengan jumlah shot yang kamu pertahankan.\n"

