# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.3 Compare hardware and simulation results {#43-compare-hardware-and-simulation-results}"
msgstr "4.3 Bandingkan hasil hardware dan simulasi {#43-compare-hardware-and-simulation-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Step 3.4, you used local simulation to preview how much PEC and TREX might improve the results. Compare that preview with the QPU results. If the simulated improvement and the hardware improvement are similar, local simulation is a useful way to evaluate mitigation settings for this workload before you spend QPU time on them.\n"
msgstr "Di Langkah 3.4, kamu memakai simulasi lokal untuk melihat gambaran seberapa besar PEC dan TREX mungkin memperbaiki hasil. Bandingkan gambaran itu dengan hasil QPU. Kalau peningkatan hasil simulasi dan hardware mirip, simulasi lokal adalah cara yang berguna untuk mengevaluasi pengaturan mitigasi untuk workload ini sebelum kamu menghabiskan waktu QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The comparison is approximate, for two reasons:\n"
msgstr "Perbandingan ini bersifat perkiraan, karena dua alasan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulations run the Cliffordized circuit from Step 3.1, while the hardware jobs run the original circuit.\n"
msgstr "Simulasi menjalankan circuit yang sudah di-Cliffordize dari Langkah 3.1, sedangkan job hardware menjalankan circuit asli.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulations use the noise model learned in Step 3.3, while the mitigated hardware job uses the noise model that was refreshed in Step 4.2.\n"
msgstr "Simulasi memakai model noise yang dipelajari di Langkah 3.3, sedangkan job hardware dengan mitigasi memakai model noise yang disegarkan di Langkah 4.2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a direct check of the noise model itself, use the comparison of the Clifford circuit results in Step 3.4.4.\n"
msgstr "Untuk pemeriksaan langsung terhadap model noise itu sendiri, gunakan perbandingan hasil circuit Clifford di Langkah 3.4.4.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/3b67439e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/profiling-tools/extracted-outputs/3b67439e-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this run, mitigation reduced the mean absolute deviation from 0.290 to 0.046 in the simulation (about a factor of six) and from 0.202 to 0.050 on the QPU (about a factor of four). In both cases, the mitigated values scatter around 1, and most of them agree with 1 within their error bars.\n"
msgstr "Pada run ini, mitigasi menurunkan rata-rata deviasi absolut dari 0,290 menjadi 0,046 dalam simulasi (sekitar enam kali lipat) dan dari 0,202 menjadi 0,050 di QPU (sekitar empat kali lipat). Dalam kedua kasus, nilai yang dimitigasi tersebar di sekitar 1, dan sebagian besar sesuai dengan 1 dalam batas error bar-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.4 Inspect execution spans {#44-inspect-execution-spans}"
msgstr "4.4 Periksa execution span {#44-inspect-execution-spans}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you submit circuits with multiple configurations, such as with gate twirling, IBM Quantum Compute Service does not necessarily run all circuit configurations at the same time. Instead, it groups them into chunks and runs one chunk per shot loop. A shot loop is a single round of execution on the quantum hardware, in which every circuit in the chunk is run for the requested number of shots.\n"
msgstr "Saat kamu mengirim circuit dengan banyak konfigurasi, seperti pada gate twirling, IBM Quantum Compute Service tidak selalu menjalankan semua konfigurasi circuit sekaligus. Sebaliknya, layanan mengelompokkannya menjadi chunk dan menjalankan satu chunk per shot loop. Shot loop adalah satu putaran eksekusi di hardware kuantum, di mana setiap circuit dalam chunk dijalankan sebanyak shot yang diminta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All jobs that are submitted to a real QPU require some classical pre-processing, such as translation into pulses that can be sent to the hardware. Because this pre-processing can be done in parallel, the service dequeues and starts multiple jobs at a time. The QPU, however, can process only one unit of work at a time. Therefore, if your job generates multiple chunks, they might be interleaved with the chunks of other users' jobs, and each chunk might have to wait for its turn on the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Semua job yang dikirim ke QPU sungguhan memerlukan pra-pemrosesan klasik, seperti penerjemahan menjadi pulse yang bisa dikirim ke hardware. Karena pra-pemrosesan ini bisa dilakukan secara paralel, layanan men-dequeue dan memulai beberapa job sekaligus. Namun, QPU hanya bisa memproses satu unit kerja pada satu waktu. Karena itu, kalau job kamu menghasilkan banyak chunk, chunk tersebut mungkin diselang-seling dengan chunk dari job pengguna lain, dan setiap chunk mungkin harus menunggu gilirannya di QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The job result metadata reports the QPU execution timing for each chunk. The following visualization shows whether there are significant gaps between the executions of the chunks in your job. If the gaps are wider than your experiment can tolerate, you might want to rerun the job, or use [session execution mode](/guides/execution-modes#session-mode), which gives your workload exclusive access to the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Metadata hasil job melaporkan timing eksekusi QPU untuk setiap chunk. Visualisasi berikut menunjukkan apakah ada jeda signifikan antara eksekusi chunk dalam job kamu. Kalau jedanya lebih lebar dari yang bisa ditoleransi eksperimenmu, kamu mungkin perlu menjalankan ulang job, atau memakai [session execution mode](/guides/execution-modes#session-mode), yang memberi workload kamu akses eksklusif ke QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refer to [View execution spans](/guides/sampler-input-output#view-execution-spans) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Lihat [View execution spans](/guides/sampler-input-output#view-execution-spans) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

